 ],
 "article": {
  "title": "The Science of Sleep: Why Rest Is Productive",
  "topic": "健康科普（睡眠科学）",
  "level": "CET-4",
  "words": 305,
  "paras": [
   "Most people treat sleep as the time they “waste” before the real day begins. Science tells a different story. During sleep, the brain sorts through the day's experiences, stores what matters and clears away what does not. Far from being idle, the sleeping body is busy repairing tissue, balancing hormones and strengthening the immune system.",
   "Researchers have found that a lack of sleep harms not only health but also performance. People who sleep fewer than six hours a night think more slowly, make more mistakes and are more likely to fall ill. One study of students showed that those who slept well before an exam remembered far more than those who stayed up all night. The brain also uses the night to wash away waste products that build up during the day, a process that may protect us from long-term illness. Memory, it turns out, is not simply built while we study; it is completed while we sleep.",
   "Modern life, however, works against rest. Screens glow late into the night, coffee keeps us awake, and the pressure to be “always on” makes sleep look like a luxury. Skipping sleep to finish a task often means doing that task badly, and then paying for it twice. Yet the habit of staying up late remains a poor bargain: we borrow a few hours of the night and pay for them with days of dull thinking and low spirits.",
   "The good news is that sleep can be improved with simple steps. Keep a regular schedule, even at weekends; dim the lights an hour before bed; keep phones out of the bedroom; and treat sleep as part of work rather than its enemy. None of these ideas is complicated, and none of them costs money. In a world that praises busyness, choosing to rest may be the most productive decision of all."
  ],
  "zh": "多数人把睡眠当成“白天开始前被浪费掉”的时间，但科学研究给出了不同的答案：睡眠时大脑在整理白天的经历，保存重要的、清除多余的；身体则在修复组织、平衡激素、增强免疫。研究发现，睡眠不足不仅伤身，更拉低表现——每晚睡不足六小时的人反应更慢、错误更多、更容易生病；考前睡好的学生，记得远比熬夜的人多。夜里大脑还会清理白天积累的代谢废物，这一过程可能帮我们远离长期疾病。可见记忆不只是在学习时“写下”，更是在睡眠中“存好”。然而现代生活处处与休息为敌：屏幕深夜发亮、咖啡让人清醒、“随时在线”的压力让睡眠像奢侈品。熬夜赶工常等于把事做糟，还要付两遍代价。好消息是，改善睡眠只需简单几步：保持规律作息（周末也一样）、睡前调暗灯光、把手机请出卧室、把睡眠当作工作的一部分。在一个推崇忙碌的世界里，选择休息，也许正是最高效的决定。",
  "hard": [
   {
    "en": "Far from being idle, the sleeping body is busy repairing tissue, balancing hormones and strengthening the immune system.",
    "cn": "睡眠中的身体非但没有闲着，反而在忙着修复组织、平衡激素、增强免疫系统。",
    "why": "“far from + 动名词”置于句首，表“非但不……反而……”的强调对比；后面三个动名词短语并列（repairing / balancing / strengthening），写作时可用来罗列多个并行动作。"
   },
   {
    "en": "Memory, it turns out, is not simply built while we study; it is completed while we sleep.",
    "cn": "事实证明，记忆不只是在我们学习时建立，更是在我们睡眠时完成。",
    "why": "“it turns out”作插入语，用逗号隔开，语气更客观；分号连接两个对比分句（not simply...; it is...），是写议论文时“先破后立”的常用句型。"
   },
   {
    "en": "In a world that praises busyness, choosing to rest may be the most productive decision of all.",
    "cn": "在一个推崇忙碌的世界里，选择休息或许才是最富成效的决定。",
    "why": "定语从句 that praises busyness 修饰 a world；动名词短语 choosing to rest 作主语，谓语用单数 may be；结尾用 of all 加强语气。此句适合放在作文末段作收束。"
   }
